    "publishedAt": "2026-11-06",
    "summary": "NVIDIA's own US marketplace, on the other hand, lists the RTX PRO 6000 for $16,000 , even though that card has more CUDA cores (24,064 vs. So even at SHI's discounted price, the cut-down card costs around $1,400 more. NVIDIA hasn't announced official pricing since it quietly added the RTX PRO 5500 to its lineup in September, so it isn't clear whether the $17,999 figure comes from NVIDIA or PNY. With orders far ahead of supply, it's reasonable to expect RTX PRO 5500 pricing to stay high for a while.",
